; Thief II VR, Quest Touch controllers (read by dinput.dll as an Xbox pad; see README_QUEST.txt).
; Appended once to user.bnd by run_quest.bat (your old user.bnd is kept as user.bnd.before-quest).
; Later lines win, so these replace any earlier binds on the same buttons. Rebind any of them in
; Options > Controls > Customize Controls, using the controllers themselves.
;   Touch            = Xbox   = game button
;   right trigger    = RT     = left mouse button (attack / draw bow), sent by dinput.dll
;   right grip       = RB     = joy5
;   A / B            = A / B  = joy1 / joy2
;   X / Y            = X / Y  = joy3 / joy4   (Y shows/hides the HUD; leave it unbound here)
;   left trigger     = LT     = joy6
;   left grip        = LB     = held: chord button (grip + another button = joy12..joy26)
;   stick clicks     = L3/R3  = joy10 / joy11 (both together = recentre the view)
;   left menu button = Esc (WinlatorXR does this itself)
joystick_enable 1
joy_rotate 0
joystick_deadzone 0.05
bind joy_axisx +joyxaxis
bind joy_axisy +joyforward
bind joy5 +use_item
bind joy1 +jumpblock
bind joy2 crouch
bind joy3 next_weapon
bind joy6 next_item
bind joy12 drop_item
bind joy13 clear_weapon
bind joy14 prev_weapon
bind joy17 prev_item
bind joy23 +leanforward
bind joy25 +leanleft
bind joy26 +leanright
